{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:01I6:title", "parent_tag": "01I6", "chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "section_title", "risk_level": "R1", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "Quasi-coherent sheaves on affines", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-quasi-coherent-affine}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:72265f149333121ecef4da103fd370b05bee1ddd42c3e5960076829b4ebcd970", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:cd932e2a6d9bb46ad147012863ede81e3bde0781e930afef8eb45d8b65c8b9b9", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:01I6:prose-0001", "parent_tag": "01I6", "chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "paragraph", "risk_level": "R2", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nRecall that we have defined the abstract notion of a quasi-coherent\nsheaf in Modules, Definition <REF_0001>.\nIn this section we show that any quasi-coherent sheaf on an affine\nscheme <MATH_0001> corresponds to the sheaf <MATH_0002> associated to\nan <MATH_0003>-module <MATH_0004>.\n\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "REF_0001": "\\ref{modules-definition-quasi-coherent}", "MATH_0001": "$\\Spec(R)$", "MATH_0002": "$\\widetilde M$", "MATH_0003": "$R$", "MATH_0004": "$M$"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:879c0606f6473e2b47d5da08da918f4aafc518e2ab2b3b61a94c7122b285b3e2", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e2667d423e861bb789b4e2974b1980c92463902d55fd16eeeacce1c8b116bcf0", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9b28276e202b0afa9ded77c04868f83c80b741a39b158e52e5ce5bb13d3bea38"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:01I7:statement", "parent_tag": "01I6", "chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "lemma", "risk_level": "R3", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001>\nbe an affine scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be an <MATH_0003>-module. There exists a canonical\nisomorphism between the sheaf <MATH_0004> associated to the <MATH_0005>-module\n<MATH_0006> (Definition <REF_0001>) and the sheaf\n<MATH_0007> associated to the <MATH_0008>-module <MATH_0009>\n(Modules, Definition <REF_0002>).\nThis isomorphism is functorial in <MATH_0010>. In particular,\nthe sheaves <MATH_0011> are quasi-coherent. Moreover, they\nare characterized by the following mapping property\n<MATH_0012>\nfor any sheaf of <MATH_0013>-modules <MATH_0014>.\nHere a map <MATH_0015> corresponds\nto its effect on global sections.\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(X, \\mathcal{O}_X) = (\\Spec(R), \\mathcal{O}_{\\Spec(R)})$", "MATH_0002": "$M$", "MATH_0003": "$R$", "MATH_0004": "$\\widetilde M$", "MATH_0005": "$R$", "MATH_0006": "$M$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{definition-structure-sheaf}", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{F}_M$", "MATH_0008": "$R$", "MATH_0009": "$M$", "REF_0002": "\\ref{modules-definition-sheaf-associated}", "MATH_0010": "$M$", "MATH_0011": "$\\widetilde M$", "MATH_0012": "$$\n\\Hom_{\\mathcal{O}_X}(\\widetilde M, \\mathcal{F})\n=\n\\Hom_R(M, \\Gamma(X, \\mathcal{F}))\n$$", "MATH_0013": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0014": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0015": "$\\alpha : \\widetilde M \\to \\mathcal{F}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-compare-constructions}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:75758c73c05a5c576d27256a39e2697370fed012f97f00477eb0517a9bfa1610", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4918d871b380b82d9377eb120b8d62dbbc68c4de6c70ad6dfcf1549a81c26e29", "source_math_hash": "sha256:dc7330e2d3b1c91b95cc2786907006f3fa29d6a828d547b482a032b4103b7784"}
{"schema_version": 1, "unit_id": "tag:01I7:proof", "parent_tag": "01I6", "chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "proof", "risk_level": "R3", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_text": "By Modules, Lemma <REF_0001>\nwe have a morphism <MATH_0001> corresponding\nto the map <MATH_0002>. Let <MATH_0003>\ncorrespond to the prime <MATH_0004>.\nThe induced map on stalks are the maps\n<MATH_0005>\nwhich are isomorphisms because\n<MATH_0006>.\nHence the map <MATH_0007> is an isomorphism.\nThe mapping property follows from the mapping property of\nthe sheaves <MATH_0008>.\n", "source_status": "CURRENT", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{modules-lemma-construct-quasi-coherent-sheaves}", "MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}_M \\to \\widetilde M$", "MATH_0002": "$M \\to \\Gamma(X, \\widetilde M) = M$", "MATH_0003": "$x \\in X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathfrak p \\subset R$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}_{X, x} \\otimes_R M \\to M_{\\mathfrak p}$", "MATH_0006": "$R_{\\mathfrak p} \\otimes_R M = M_{\\mathfrak p}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{F}_M \\to \\widetilde M$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{F}_M$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "source_text_hash": "sha256:cdb38c2deaedd0f93bbe594f89c6537cf1c9bbaf741b9990e575d485acd23c89", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:3efca27f4def4e59e78adf1e4f20006417d21766db4018b72f7de89b91d86f7f", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a5f7dd8a3c68308064a6c7d19d43f6e4d154eb715c118a55bcf64aa54b5c46dd"}
